        },
        {
          "line": 47,
          "text": "Every right-hand side has support in the closed causal cone. Hence compactly supported tests whose supports are spacelike separated in the stated Minkowski sense give commuting field-strength operators on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$. The quotient representation of [[lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum]] makes these smeared field strengths Lorentz covariant: their on-shell coefficient depends on a polarization class only through $p_a\\epsilon_b-p_b\\epsilon_a$. These conclusions concern gauge-invariant free observables and do not assert locality of the Coulomb potential."
        },
        {
          "line": 57,
          "text": "[F2] On the future cone, the quotient sections are identified with $\\mathcal H_T$ by $u(\\mathbf k)=T_p[s(p)]/\\sqrt{2\\omega}$, where $T_p[\\epsilon]=\\boldsymbol\\epsilon-(\\mathbf k/\\omega)\\epsilon^0$; the Lorentz action is induced by $[\\epsilon(p)]\\mapsto[\\Lambda\\epsilon(\\Lambda^{-1}p)]$. [[lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum]]"
        }
      ],
      "norm_separability_context": [
        {
          "line": 77,
          "text": "3.1 If a test function is supported in the complement of $\\operatorname{supp}C_0$, each of its derivatives has support contained in that of the test function, and the definition $\\langle\\partial_a C_0,f\\rangle=-\\langle C_0,\\partial_af\\rangle$ shows the derivative distribution also vanishes there. Thus every derivative in step 2.2 remains supported in the closed causal cone from [F3]. For spacelike-separated compact test supports, every point in their difference set lies outside that cone, so pairing each commutator with their tensor product gives zero. The smeared field strengths commute on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$. [F3, step 2.2, given] \u220e"
        }
      ]
    },
